    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Across several wealth-management firms, AI in advice delivery spans advisor-facing assistants and lead-matching, client-facing assistants, and search/summarization tools.",
        "chunk_ids": [
          "MS-TR-2025Q3#8",
          "RJF-TR-2025Q4#5",
          "SCHW-PR-2026-10-15-01#3",
          "BAC-TR-2026Q2#21"
        ],
        "part_id": "a1.all"
      },
      {
        "text": "The most common specific use cases are preparing advisors for client conversations, summarizing meetings, drafting communications, and matching advisors to prospects.",
        "chunk_ids": [
          "BAC-TR-2026Q2#6",
          "MS-TR-2025Q4#35",
          "DELOITTE-AGENTIC-2026#2",
          "SCHW-TR-2026Q1#18"
        ],
        "part_id": "a2.all"
      },
      {
        "text": "Firms consistently say AI augments rather than replaces human advisors, positioning it to free up time and deepen client relationships.",
        "chunk_ids": [
          "BAC-TR-2025Q3#65",
          "RJF-TR-2025Q2#8",
          "SCHW-TR-2026Q2#19",
          "MS-TR-2026Q3#35"
        ],
        "part_id": "a3.all"
      },
      {
        "text": "Morgan Stanley's CEO makes the strongest claim, calling AI 'existentially important' and 'absolutely the top priority for the firm as the adviser,' and saying the firm is now 'double overweight' in AI.",
        "chunk_ids": [
          "MS-TR-2026Q3#49"
        ],
        "part_id": "a4.all"
      },
      {
        "text": "Raymond James reports 6,500 unique users and a 99.5% satisfaction rate for its Raimond AI assistant, while Schwab reports over 220 AI use cases.",
        "chunk_ids": [
          "RJF-TR-2026Q2#33",
          "SCHW-TR-2025Q4#18"
        ],
        "part_id": "a5.all"
      },
      {
        "text": "On this evidence the comparison can be made: Morgan Stanley's CEO goes furthest by naming AI the firm's top priority and existentially important, language none of the other firms match.",
